WEBVTT

00:00:00.251 --> 00:00:03.293
Oxford Bookworms, Stage 1.

00:00:03.353 --> 00:00:06.415
The Wizard of Oz, by L.

00:00:06.475 --> 00:00:13.038
Frank Baume, retold by Rosemary Border, read by Jennifer J.

00:00:13.078 --> 00:00:15.160
Myers.

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:42.802
Chapter 1 The Cyclone Dorothy lived in a small house in Kansas with Uncle Henry, Aunt Emma, and a little black dog called Toto.

00:00:42.863 --> 00:00:51.716
There were no trees and no hills in Kansas, and it was often very windy.

00:00:51.776 --> 00:01:09.140
Sometimes the wind came very fast and very suddenly That was a cyclone, and it could blow trees and people and buildings away.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:23.495
There were cellars under all the houses, and when a cyclone came, people went down into their cellars and stayed there.

00:01:23.555 --> 00:01:29.790
Uncle Henry came out and looked up at the sky.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:34.702
Then he ran quickly back into the house.

00:01:34.762 --> 00:01:37.353
There is a cyclone coming.

00:01:37.413 --> 00:01:40.015
He called to Aunt Em and Dorothy.

00:01:40.074 --> 00:01:43.526
We must go down into the cellar.

00:01:43.586 --> 00:01:51.920
They ran to the door of the cellar, but Toto was afraid, and he ran under the bed.

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:54.605
Dorothy ran after him.

00:01:54.665 --> 00:01:58.630
Quick, shouted Aunt M from the cellar.

00:01:58.690 --> 00:02:03.024
Leave the dog and come down into the cellar.

00:02:03.084 --> 00:02:08.618
Dorothy picked up Toto and ran to the cellar door.

00:02:08.678 --> 00:02:14.662
But before she got there, the cyclone hit the house.

00:02:14.722 --> 00:02:20.847
And then a very strange thing happened.

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:23.681
The house moved.

00:02:23.741 --> 00:02:33.216
And then it went slowly up, up, up into the sky.

00:02:33.276 --> 00:02:39.968
And M and Uncle Henry were down in the cellar under the ground.

00:02:40.028 --> 00:02:48.980
But the house, Dorothy and Toto went up to the top of the cyclone.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:53.590
Dorothy looked through the open cellar door.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:59.934
and saw hills and houses a long way down.

00:02:59.993 --> 00:03:04.638
She closed the cellar door quickly.

00:03:04.698 --> 00:03:10.583
The wind blew the house along for many hours.

00:03:10.643 --> 00:03:15.076
At first, Dorothy was afraid.

00:03:15.136 --> 00:03:23.778
But we can't do anything about it," she said to Toto, so let's wait and see.

00:03:23.838 --> 00:03:31.610
And after two or three hours, she and Toto went to sleep.

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:41.291
When Dorothy opened her eyes again, the house was on the ground, and everything was quiet.

00:03:41.351 --> 00:03:47.740
She picked up Toto, opened the door, and went out.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:57.754
They saw tall trees and beautiful flowers and little houses with blue doors.

00:03:57.814 --> 00:04:01.186
Dorothy gave a little cry.

00:04:01.246 --> 00:04:04.357
This is in Kansas, Toto.

00:04:04.417 --> 00:04:07.538
And who are these people?

00:04:07.598 --> 00:04:15.914
There were three very short men in blue hats, coats and trousers.

00:04:15.974 --> 00:04:21.560
and a little old woman in a beautiful white dress.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:33.086
The woman walked up to Dorothy and said, thank you, thank you, now the people are free.

00:04:33.145 --> 00:04:36.137
Why are you thanking me?

00:04:36.197 --> 00:04:41.490
Dorothy asked, you killed the witch of the East.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:45.412
Said the woman, she was a bad witch.

00:04:45.472 --> 00:04:50.917
and her people, the munchkins, were very afraid of her.

00:04:50.976 --> 00:04:58.822
Now she is dead, and we and the munchkins want to thank you.

00:04:58.882 --> 00:05:11.108
The little old woman and the three little men all smiled happily at Dorothy, but Dorothy did not understand.

00:05:11.168 --> 00:05:16.278
But I didn't kill anybody, she said.

00:05:16.338 --> 00:05:19.941
Your house fell on the witch.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.072
Laughed the little woman.

00:05:22.132 --> 00:05:26.306
Look, you can see her feet.

00:05:26.366 --> 00:05:34.733
Dorothy looked and saw two feet with red shoes under the house.

00:05:34.793 --> 00:05:40.282
Suddenly, one of the munchkins gave a shout.

00:05:40.342 --> 00:05:45.620
Her feet are disappearing in the hot sun.

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:51.734
A second later, there were only the red shoes.

00:05:51.794 --> 00:05:55.487
Good, said the little woman.

00:05:55.546 --> 00:06:00.100
She picked up the shoes and gave them to Dorothy.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:02.682
They're your shoes now.

00:06:02.742 --> 00:06:04.934
You must wear them.

00:06:04.994 --> 00:06:12.168
Because a witch's shoes can sometimes do wonderful things.

00:06:12.228 --> 00:06:15.860
Thank you, said Dorothy.

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:18.540
But who are you?

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:20.912
Are you a munchkin?

00:06:20.972 --> 00:06:24.593
No, but I'm their friend.

00:06:24.653 --> 00:06:31.976
I'm the witch of the North, and I came to see the dead witch of the East.

00:06:32.036 --> 00:06:34.453
But don't be afraid.

00:06:34.513 --> 00:06:37.080
I'm a good witch.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:41.764
But Aunt M says there are Denny witches.

00:06:41.823 --> 00:06:45.806
Oh yes, there are, said the witch.

00:06:45.866 --> 00:06:51.739
Here in the country of Oz, we have four witches.

00:06:51.799 --> 00:06:57.132
The witches of the North and the South are good witches.

00:06:57.192 --> 00:07:03.008
But those of the East and the West are bad witches.

00:07:03.068 --> 00:07:11.927
Now the Witch of the East is dead, so there is only one bad witch.

00:07:11.986 --> 00:07:15.619
We have a famous wizard too.

00:07:15.679 --> 00:07:23.695
We call him the Wizard of Oz, and he lives in the Emerald City.

00:07:23.715 --> 00:07:31.414
How many witches and wizards do you have in your country?

00:07:31.474 --> 00:07:35.818
We don't have any," said Dorothy.

00:07:35.878 --> 00:07:40.990
Suddenly she remembered Aunt Anne and Uncle Henry.

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:44.682
How can I get back home to Kansas?

00:07:44.742 --> 00:07:46.482
She asked.

00:07:46.542 --> 00:07:49.364
Where is Kansas?

00:07:49.424 --> 00:07:51.444
asked the good witch.

00:07:51.504 --> 00:07:59.037
I don't know what country called Kansas, so I can't tell you the way.

00:07:59.097 --> 00:08:02.313
Dorothy began to cry.

00:08:02.373 --> 00:08:06.330
Oh dear, what can I do?

00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:10.691
Please don't cry, said the witch.

00:08:10.751 --> 00:08:14.272
Go and see the Wizard of Oz.

00:08:14.332 --> 00:08:19.504
He's a good wizard, and perhaps he can help you.

00:08:19.564 --> 00:08:24.106
It's a long way, and you must walk there.

00:08:24.166 --> 00:08:30.610
I can't go with you, but I can give you my kiss.

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:34.504
She gave Dorothy a little kiss.

00:08:34.564 --> 00:08:39.686
It looked like a small red flower on Dorothy's face.

00:08:39.746 --> 00:08:44.920
Now, nothing can hurt you, she said.

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:50.062
Look, there is the road to the Emerald City.

00:08:50.123 --> 00:08:56.466
It is made of yellow bricks, so you cannot lose your way.

00:08:56.526 --> 00:08:58.507
Goodbye.

00:08:58.567 --> 00:09:00.448
Goodbye.

00:09:00.508 --> 00:09:03.738
said the three little munchkins.

00:09:03.798 --> 00:09:12.420
In the house Dorothy found some bread and some apples and she put them all in a bag.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:16.871
Then she put on her blue and white dress.

00:09:16.931 --> 00:09:20.702
Now I look nice, she said.

00:09:20.762 --> 00:09:24.133
She looked down at her old shoes.

00:09:24.193 --> 00:09:30.458
Then she remembered the bad witches red shoes and put them on.

00:09:30.518 --> 00:09:33.464
She picked up her bag of food.

00:09:33.524 --> 00:09:36.317
Come on, Toto, she called.

00:09:36.377 --> 00:09:39.040
We are going to find the Wizard of Oz.

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:40.771
Chapter 2.

00:09:40.831 --> 00:10:04.207
The Yellow Brick Road Dorothy and Toto walked along the yellow brick road for a long time.

00:10:04.267 --> 00:10:09.758
When they were tired, they stopped in a field by the road.

00:10:09.818 --> 00:10:18.680
Not far away, there was a scarecrow, and Dorothy and Toto walked across to look at it.

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:23.251
Good day, said the scarecrow.

00:10:23.311 --> 00:10:28.054
Oh, said Dorothy, you can speak.

00:10:28.113 --> 00:10:33.100
Of course I can speak," said the Scarecrow.

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:38.014
But I can't move up here on this pole.

00:10:38.074 --> 00:10:40.386
I'd like to get down.

00:10:40.446 --> 00:10:42.789
Can you help me?

00:10:42.849 --> 00:10:48.654
Carefully, Dorothy took the Scarecrow off his pole.

00:10:48.714 --> 00:10:51.256
Thank you very much.

00:10:51.316 --> 00:10:53.256
said the Scarecrow.

00:10:53.316 --> 00:10:59.260
He moved his arms and legs and straw went everywhere.

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:01.012
Who are you?

00:11:01.072 --> 00:11:04.945
He asked, and where are you going?

00:11:05.004 --> 00:11:10.479
I'm Dorothy, and I'm going to the Emerald City.

00:11:10.539 --> 00:11:16.234
I want to go home to Kansas, but I don't know the way.

00:11:16.294 --> 00:11:20.602
I'm going to ask the Wizard of Oz for help.

00:11:20.662 --> 00:11:23.589
Where is the Emerald City?"

00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:25.721
asked the Scarecrow.

00:11:25.781 --> 00:11:29.063
And who is the Wizard of Oz?

00:11:29.123 --> 00:11:36.388
I don't know anything, you see, because I have no brains in my head.

00:11:36.448 --> 00:11:38.740
Only straw.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:40.610
Oh, dear!

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:42.162
said Dorothy.

00:11:42.222 --> 00:11:44.487
I'm very sorry.

00:11:44.547 --> 00:11:50.646
I would very much like to have some brains," the Scarecrow said.

00:11:50.706 --> 00:11:54.600
Can I go to the Emerald City with you?

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:59.073
Perhaps the Wizard of Oz can give me some brains.

00:11:59.133 --> 00:12:01.344
What do you think?

00:12:01.404 --> 00:12:04.818
I don't know, said Dorothy.

00:12:04.878 --> 00:12:08.260
But yes, please, come with me.

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:13.472
He's a famous wizard, so perhaps he can help you.

00:12:13.532 --> 00:12:17.264
She felt very sorry for the Scarecrow.

00:12:17.324 --> 00:12:21.106
Don't be afraid of Toto, she said.

00:12:21.166 --> 00:12:23.746
He never hurts people.

00:12:23.806 --> 00:12:27.888
Nothing can hurt me, said the Scarecrow.

00:12:27.948 --> 00:12:30.410
I'm not afraid of anything.

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:33.220
Well, that's not true.

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:37.256
I am afraid of fire, of course.

00:12:37.316 --> 00:12:42.132
Dorothy walked along the road with her new friend.

00:12:42.192 --> 00:12:52.328
Soon she began to feel hungry, so she sat down and she and Toto ate some bread and apples.

00:12:52.388 --> 00:12:55.108
Would you like some scarecrow?

00:12:55.168 --> 00:12:56.640
said Dorothy.

00:12:56.700 --> 00:13:00.151
No, thank you, said the scarecrow.

00:13:00.211 --> 00:13:02.993
I don't need to eat or drink.

00:13:03.052 --> 00:13:05.794
You can't eat when you're made of straw.

00:13:05.814 --> 00:13:06.970
No.

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:10.787
Tell me about your home."

00:13:10.847 --> 00:13:19.040
So Dorothy told him about Kansas, an Uncle Henry in Aunt Anne, and the cyclone.

00:13:19.100 --> 00:13:23.351
But why do you want to leave this beautiful country?

00:13:23.411 --> 00:13:25.252
Ask the Scarecrow.

00:13:25.312 --> 00:13:31.334
Kansas, you say, has no trees, no green hills.

00:13:31.394 --> 00:13:33.316
No gardens.

00:13:33.376 --> 00:13:36.027
I don't understand.

00:13:36.088 --> 00:13:41.260
That's because you have no brains, said Dorothy.

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:44.062
Kansas is my home.

00:13:44.122 --> 00:13:49.144
We say East, West, home's best.

00:13:49.204 --> 00:13:51.055
And it's true.

00:13:51.115 --> 00:13:54.356
I want to go home.

00:13:54.416 --> 00:14:01.213
They walked along the road for some hours, and then it got dark.

00:14:01.273 --> 00:14:09.072
Dorothy was tired, and soon the scarecrow saw a little house behind some trees.

00:14:09.132 --> 00:14:13.326
There was nobody there, so they went in.

00:14:13.386 --> 00:14:21.162
Dorothy and Toto slept, but the scarecrow just stood all night with his eyes open.

00:14:21.222 --> 00:14:25.547
Scarecrows don't sleep, he said.

00:14:25.607 --> 00:14:29.744
In the morning Dorothy looked for water.

00:14:29.804 --> 00:14:32.188
Why do you want water?"

00:14:32.248 --> 00:14:34.418
asked the scarecrow.

00:14:34.478 --> 00:14:39.510
Toto and I are thirsty, and I need to wash.

00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:43.701
I'm sorry for you, said the scarecrow.

00:14:43.761 --> 00:14:54.134
You need a lot of things, but you have brains, and you can think, and that's wonderful.

00:14:54.194 --> 00:14:58.671
They found some water, and Dorothy washed.

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:02.628
Then she and Toto ate some bread.

00:15:02.688 --> 00:15:12.484
Suddenly, they heard a shout from the trees near the house, and they all ran out of the house to look.

00:15:12.544 --> 00:15:18.750
They saw a man by a big tree with an axe in his hand.

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:21.361
He was made of tin.

00:15:21.421 --> 00:15:25.424
He stood very still and shouted, Oh!

00:15:25.484 --> 00:15:28.849
again and again.

00:15:28.909 --> 00:15:32.196
What can I do for you?"

00:15:32.256 --> 00:15:34.188
asked Dorothy.

00:15:34.248 --> 00:15:36.530
I can't move.

00:15:36.590 --> 00:15:38.162
Said the Tin Man.

00:15:38.222 --> 00:15:40.924
Please oil me.

00:15:40.984 --> 00:15:45.104
There's an oil can in my house.

00:15:45.164 --> 00:15:51.783
at once Dorothy ran back to the house and found the oil can.

00:15:51.843 --> 00:16:00.328
Then she came back and with the scarecrow's help she carefully oiled the tin man.

00:16:00.388 --> 00:16:09.555
Slowly he began to move, first his head and then his arms and legs.

00:16:09.616 --> 00:16:12.798
Thank you, he said.

00:16:12.858 --> 00:16:15.647
I feel better now.

00:16:15.707 --> 00:16:18.786
he put down his axe.

00:16:18.846 --> 00:16:27.343
I went out in the rain, you see, and water is very bad for a tin body.

00:16:27.363 --> 00:16:35.950
I was there for a long time, and nobody came to help me.

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:44.281
We stopped at your house for the night, Dorothy said, and we heard your shouts this morning.

00:16:44.341 --> 00:16:47.249
Where are you going?

00:16:47.309 --> 00:16:49.230
asked the Tin Man.

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:53.954
So Dorothy told him about the Wizard of Oz.

00:16:53.974 --> 00:17:00.570
I want to go back to Kansas, and the Scarecrow wants some brains, she said.

00:17:00.630 --> 00:17:04.322
The Tin Man was very interested.

00:17:04.382 --> 00:17:07.825
Can the Wizard give me a heart?

00:17:07.886 --> 00:17:09.206
Do you think?

00:17:09.266 --> 00:17:13.666
I have no heart, so I can't love.

00:17:13.726 --> 00:17:19.643
or feel, I would very much like to have a heart.

00:17:19.703 --> 00:17:23.404
Come with us, said the scarecrow.

00:17:23.464 --> 00:17:30.756
Yes, said Dorothy, and then you can ask the wizard for help too.

00:17:30.816 --> 00:17:36.038
So they all walked along the yellow brick road.

00:17:36.098 --> 00:17:40.479
There were many tall trees next to the road.

00:17:40.539 --> 00:17:48.070
And sometimes the three friends heard noises from animals behind the trees.

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:53.072
Dorothy did not like these noises very much.

00:17:53.132 --> 00:17:56.783
How far is it to the Emerald City?

00:17:56.843 --> 00:17:58.704
She asked the Tin Man.

00:17:58.764 --> 00:18:00.504
Do you know?

00:18:00.564 --> 00:18:05.506
It's a long way, I think, said the Tin Man.

00:18:05.566 --> 00:18:17.608
And we must be careful because But just then a big lion suddenly ran out from the trees into the road.

00:18:17.668 --> 00:18:19.839
It opened its mouth.

00:18:19.899 --> 00:18:26.012
It had long yellow teeth and began to run after Toto.

00:18:26.072 --> 00:18:29.024
Dorothy was afraid for Toto.

00:18:29.084 --> 00:18:34.606
She ran up to the lion and hit it on the nose with her bag.

00:18:34.666 --> 00:18:37.468
Don't hurt my dog.

00:18:37.528 --> 00:18:39.374
She cried angrily.

00:18:39.434 --> 00:18:41.271
He's smaller than you.

00:18:41.291 --> 00:18:45.183
I didn't hurt him.

00:18:45.243 --> 00:18:46.904
Said the lion.

00:18:46.964 --> 00:18:48.975
Don't hit me again.

00:18:49.035 --> 00:18:50.616
Please.

00:18:50.676 --> 00:18:51.957
Why?

00:18:52.017 --> 00:18:53.738
You're afraid.

00:18:53.798 --> 00:18:55.358
Said Dorothy.

00:18:55.418 --> 00:18:57.490
Be quiet, Toto.

00:18:57.550 --> 00:18:59.341
He isn't going to hurt you.

00:18:59.361 --> 00:19:02.102
He's more afraid than you are.

00:19:02.162 --> 00:19:05.034
He's just a big coward.

00:19:05.094 --> 00:19:06.782
It's true.

00:19:06.842 --> 00:19:08.390
said the lion.

00:19:08.451 --> 00:19:10.922
I am a coward.

00:19:10.982 --> 00:19:14.244
Everyone thinks lions are brave.

00:19:14.264 --> 00:19:19.696
I make a lot of noise, but I'm not brave.

00:19:19.756 --> 00:19:22.728
I'm just a coward.

00:19:22.788 --> 00:19:27.300
And the cowardly lion began to cry.

00:19:27.360 --> 00:19:32.473
Then Dorothy told him about the Wizard of Oz.

00:19:32.533 --> 00:19:36.823
Come with us to the Emerald City, she said.

00:19:36.883 --> 00:19:39.923
I want to go back to Kansas.

00:19:39.984 --> 00:19:46.098
The scarecrow wants some brains, and the tin man wants a heart.

00:19:46.158 --> 00:19:50.672
Perhaps the Wizard of Oz can make you brave.

00:19:50.732 --> 00:19:53.374
Oh, thank you.

00:19:53.434 --> 00:19:55.146
Said the lion.

00:19:55.206 --> 00:19:59.400
I would very much like to be brave.

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:03.690
And so the cowardly lion came with them.

00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:12.320
At first, Toto was afraid of him, but very soon he and the lion were good friends.

00:20:12.380 --> 00:20:23.404
That night, Dorothy and Toto slept under a big tree, next to the cowardly lion's big, warm body.

00:20:23.464 --> 00:20:29.640
In the morning, they ate the last of their bread.

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:34.905
What are we going to eat for dinner?"

00:20:34.966 --> 00:20:38.837
I can kill an animal for you.

00:20:38.897 --> 00:20:41.798
Said the cowardly lion.

00:20:41.858 --> 00:20:43.689
Oh, no.

00:20:43.749 --> 00:20:47.361
Please, don't kill anything.

00:20:47.421 --> 00:20:49.402
The tin man said.

00:20:49.462 --> 00:20:51.803
He began to cry.

00:20:51.863 --> 00:20:56.455
We don't want to hurt any animals.

00:20:56.475 --> 00:21:01.326
I haven't got a heart, but I feel sorry for them.

00:21:01.386 --> 00:21:06.728
Dorothy quickly got out the oil can and oiled his face.

00:21:06.788 --> 00:21:09.510
Don't cry, she said.

00:21:09.570 --> 00:21:13.212
You know water is bad for you.

00:21:13.272 --> 00:21:21.386
They walked along the yellow road, and after an hour or two, they came to a big river.

00:21:21.446 --> 00:21:24.588
Oh no, said Dorothy.

00:21:24.648 --> 00:21:27.330
How can we get across?

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:30.854
The lion looked down at the river.

00:21:30.914 --> 00:21:35.668
I'm very afraid of falling," he said.

00:21:35.728 --> 00:21:40.181
But I think I can jump across.

00:21:40.241 --> 00:21:43.713
Good, said the Scarecrow at once.

00:21:43.773 --> 00:21:48.506
You can carry us on your back, one at a time.

00:21:48.566 --> 00:21:58.218
So the cowardly lion jumped across the river, first with the Scarecrow on his back, then with Dorothy and Toto.

00:21:58.278 --> 00:22:01.264
and last with the tin man.

00:22:01.324 --> 00:22:05.435
But soon they came to a second river.

00:22:05.495 --> 00:22:11.818
This one was very big, and the lion could not jump across it.

00:22:11.878 --> 00:22:14.970
The scarecrow thought for a minute.

00:22:15.030 --> 00:22:17.290
Look, he said.

00:22:17.350 --> 00:22:24.832
There's a tall tree next to the river, but tin man can cut it down with his axe.

00:22:24.892 --> 00:22:31.226
And when the tree falls across the river, we can walk across the tree.

00:22:31.286 --> 00:22:40.802
Very good, said the lion, for somebody with straw in their head and not brains.

00:22:40.862 --> 00:22:54.012
So the tin man cut down the tree with his axe, and soon they were all across that river too.

00:22:54.072 --> 00:23:09.472
Chapter 3 The Emerald City It was a long day.

00:23:09.532 --> 00:23:17.478
The yellow brick road went past fields and through trees, up hills and down hills.

00:23:17.538 --> 00:23:23.772
In the evening they began to see small green houses by the road.

00:23:23.832 --> 00:23:30.266
Sometimes little people in green clothes came out and looked at the friends.

00:23:30.327 --> 00:23:37.222
But they did not come near them because they were afraid of the cowardly lion.

00:23:37.282 --> 00:23:40.123
Everything here is green.

00:23:40.183 --> 00:23:44.776
Perhaps we're near the Emerald City, said Dorothy.

00:23:44.836 --> 00:23:47.658
Toto and I are hungry.

00:23:47.718 --> 00:23:50.890
Let's stop at the next house.

00:23:50.950 --> 00:23:53.975
A little woman opened the door.

00:23:54.035 --> 00:24:00.282
And Dorothy said, please, can we stay the night in your house?

00:24:00.342 --> 00:24:10.627
The little woman looked at the lion, and Dorothy said quickly, the lion is my friend, and he never hurts anybody.

00:24:10.688 --> 00:24:12.228
All right.

00:24:12.288 --> 00:24:16.732
The little woman said, you can all come in.

00:24:16.792 --> 00:24:20.794
She put a wonderful dinner on the table.

00:24:20.854 --> 00:24:23.806
Dorothy and Toto ate a lot of it.

00:24:23.866 --> 00:24:30.559
and the lion ate some of it, but the scarecrow and the tin man ate nothing.

00:24:30.620 --> 00:24:33.341
Where are you all going?

00:24:33.401 --> 00:24:35.462
asked the little woman.

00:24:35.522 --> 00:24:43.035
To the Emerald City, said Dorothy, we want to see the Wizard of Oz.

00:24:43.095 --> 00:24:46.596
That's not easy, said the woman.

00:24:46.656 --> 00:24:53.514
The wizard never goes out of his house, and nobody sees his face.

00:24:53.574 --> 00:24:56.550
Is the wizard a man?

00:24:56.610 --> 00:24:58.501
asked the scarecrow.

00:24:58.561 --> 00:25:01.951
Nobody knows, said the woman.

00:25:02.011 --> 00:25:09.463
He's a wizard, so he can be a man or an animal or anything.

00:25:09.483 --> 00:25:18.554
How strange, said Dorothy, but we need his help, so we must see him.

00:25:18.614 --> 00:25:25.908
The next day, they thanked the woman, left the house, and began walking again.

00:25:25.969 --> 00:25:30.622
Soon they saw a beautiful city in front of them.

00:25:30.682 --> 00:25:35.446
It was the Emerald City at last.

00:25:35.506 --> 00:25:42.950
The friends went up the yellow brick road to a big green door and stopped.

00:25:43.010 --> 00:25:50.836
Slowly the door opened and a little man in green clothes stood there.

00:25:50.896 --> 00:25:53.865
We want to see the wizard please.

00:25:53.925 --> 00:25:55.633
said Dorothy.

00:25:55.693 --> 00:25:59.866
Nobody sees the wizard, he said.

00:25:59.926 --> 00:26:06.881
He is a very good and very famous wizard, but nobody can see him.

00:26:06.941 --> 00:26:10.814
We must see him, said Dorothy.

00:26:10.874 --> 00:26:13.466
Please ask him.

00:26:13.526 --> 00:26:17.228
All right, said the green man.

00:26:17.288 --> 00:26:19.794
I can take you to his house.

00:26:19.854 --> 00:26:24.952
But first, you must all put glasses on.

00:26:25.012 --> 00:26:28.296
He opened a big box.

00:26:28.356 --> 00:26:31.638
In it were lots of glasses.

00:26:31.698 --> 00:26:37.203
You must wear your glasses all the time, he said.

00:26:37.263 --> 00:26:40.946
Everybody in the city must wear glasses.

00:26:41.006 --> 00:26:43.492
The wizard says this.

00:26:43.552 --> 00:26:46.828
So they all put on glasses.

00:26:46.888 --> 00:26:50.520
The green man put on some glasses too.

00:26:50.580 --> 00:26:55.112
And then he took them through the Emerald City.

00:26:55.173 --> 00:26:58.364
Everything in the city was green.

00:26:58.424 --> 00:27:06.518
Men, women, children, houses, shops, streets.

00:27:06.578 --> 00:27:11.647
The green man took them to a very big house.

00:27:11.707 --> 00:27:15.354
and they went into a long green room.

00:27:15.414 --> 00:27:18.114
Wait here, he said.

00:27:18.174 --> 00:27:21.715
After a short time, he came back.

00:27:21.775 --> 00:27:30.656
You can see the wizard, he said, but you must go to him one by one.

00:27:30.716 --> 00:27:34.787
He wants to see the little girl first.

00:27:34.847 --> 00:27:40.558
Then he went away and a green girl came in.

00:27:40.618 --> 00:27:44.710
She took Dorothy to a tall green door.

00:27:44.770 --> 00:27:49.052
The wizard is in there, said the green girl.

00:27:49.072 --> 00:27:51.604
He's waiting for you.

00:27:51.664 --> 00:27:53.826
Dorothy went in.

00:27:53.886 --> 00:27:58.799
On a green chair was a very, very big head.

00:27:58.819 --> 00:28:05.323
There was no body or arms or legs, only a head.

00:28:05.343 --> 00:28:13.703
Its mouth opened and the head said, I am Oz.

00:28:13.763 --> 00:28:16.354
Who are you?

00:28:16.414 --> 00:28:20.167
And what do you want?

00:28:20.227 --> 00:28:25.500
I am Dorothy, said the child bravely.

00:28:25.560 --> 00:28:31.054
Where did you get those red shoes?

00:28:31.114 --> 00:28:35.426
From the Bad Witch of the East, said Dorothy.

00:28:35.486 --> 00:28:38.926
My house fell on her and killed her.

00:28:38.986 --> 00:28:43.626
What is that thing on your face?

00:28:43.686 --> 00:28:45.298
A kiss.

00:28:45.358 --> 00:28:49.510
The good witch of the North kissed me, said Dorothy.

00:28:49.570 --> 00:28:53.724
I need help, and she told me about you.

00:28:53.784 --> 00:28:57.878
And what do you want?

00:28:57.938 --> 00:29:03.162
I want to go home to Kansas, answer Dorothy.

00:29:03.221 --> 00:29:05.463
But I don't know the way.

00:29:05.523 --> 00:29:08.905
Please help me to get home.

00:29:08.965 --> 00:29:15.750
The big eyes opened and closed, opened and closed.

00:29:15.810 --> 00:29:20.854
Then the mouth opened and the head spoke again.

00:29:20.914 --> 00:29:33.764
Well, it said, perhaps I can help you, but first you must do something for me.

00:29:33.824 --> 00:29:38.060
What do you want me to do, asked Dorothy?

00:29:38.120 --> 00:29:42.212
Kill the bad witch of the West.

00:29:42.272 --> 00:29:47.543
But I don't want to kill anybody, said Dorothy.

00:29:47.603 --> 00:29:53.995
You killed her sister and you are wearing her shoes.

00:29:54.055 --> 00:30:00.316
Go now and kill the witch of the West.

00:30:00.376 --> 00:30:04.077
The little girl began to cry.

00:30:04.137 --> 00:30:07.298
But how can I kill the witch?

00:30:07.358 --> 00:30:09.048
She said.

00:30:09.108 --> 00:30:16.451
The big eyes opened and looked at her, but the head did not answer.

00:30:16.511 --> 00:30:22.494
Dorothy went away, and then her friends went into the wizard's room.

00:30:22.554 --> 00:30:30.080
First the scarecrow, then the tin man, and last the lion.

00:30:30.140 --> 00:30:36.253
Later they all met in the long green room and talked.

00:30:36.313 --> 00:30:40.134
Dorothy told her friends about the head.

00:30:40.194 --> 00:30:44.336
That's interesting," said the Scarecrow.

00:30:44.396 --> 00:30:46.799
I didn't see a head.

00:30:46.860 --> 00:30:49.982
I saw a beautiful woman.

00:30:50.042 --> 00:31:01.698
I asked her for some brains, and she said, yes, but first you must help Dorothy to kill the Witch of the West.

00:31:01.759 --> 00:31:08.826
I saw a big animal with two heads, said the tin man.

00:31:08.886 --> 00:31:11.088
I asked for a heart.

00:31:11.148 --> 00:31:15.290
The animal said, I can give you a heart.

00:31:15.350 --> 00:31:21.982
But first, you must help Dorothy to kill the witch of the West.

00:31:22.042 --> 00:31:25.074
What did you see, lion?

00:31:25.134 --> 00:31:31.460
I saw a ball of fire, said the cowardly lion.

00:31:31.520 --> 00:31:35.267
I said, I'm a coward.

00:31:35.327 --> 00:31:38.248
Please make me brave."

00:31:38.308 --> 00:31:47.034
And the fire said, when the witch of the West is dead, I can help you, but not before.

00:31:47.094 --> 00:31:56.969
I was angry then, said the lion, but the ball of fire got bigger and bigger, so I ran away.

00:31:56.989 --> 00:32:01.710
Oh, what are we going to do?

00:32:01.770 --> 00:32:03.339
said Dorothy.

00:32:03.399 --> 00:32:11.071
Well, said the Scarecrow, we must find the Witch of the West, and then we must kill her.

00:32:11.091 --> 00:32:33.665
Chapter 4 The Witch and the Monkey The next morning they left the Emerald City.

00:32:33.725 --> 00:32:41.540
The green man took away their glasses and told them the way to the witch's house.

00:32:41.600 --> 00:32:45.954
Everybody is afraid of the witch of the West.

00:32:46.014 --> 00:32:50.548
He said, so be careful.

00:32:50.608 --> 00:32:54.480
The friends walked for a long time.

00:32:54.540 --> 00:32:58.745
The road was bad and there were no houses.

00:32:58.805 --> 00:33:02.378
no fields, no trees.

00:33:02.438 --> 00:33:09.921
Now the Witch of the West had a magic eye, and it could see everything.

00:33:09.981 --> 00:33:16.153
She saw the friends on the road, and she was angry.

00:33:16.213 --> 00:33:24.816
She put on her tall black hat and shouted, magic monkeys, come!

00:33:24.876 --> 00:33:30.696
In a second, Forty monkeys arrived at her tall house.

00:33:30.756 --> 00:33:32.406
What do you want?

00:33:32.466 --> 00:33:34.428
They asked.

00:33:34.488 --> 00:33:41.562
There are three people, a dog, and a lion on my road.

00:33:41.622 --> 00:33:45.455
She said, kill the people and the dog.

00:33:45.515 --> 00:33:49.618
But bring the lion here to my house.

00:33:49.678 --> 00:33:52.960
He can work for me.

00:33:53.020 --> 00:33:56.216
At once said the monkey.

00:33:56.276 --> 00:33:58.652
and away they went.

00:33:58.712 --> 00:34:02.966
They broke the tin man's arms and legs.

00:34:03.026 --> 00:34:10.864
They took all the straw out of the scarecrow and threw his clothes up into a tall tree.

00:34:10.924 --> 00:34:19.503
Then they took the lion and carried him to a dark cellar under the witch's house.

00:34:19.564 --> 00:34:27.179
but they could not hurt Dorothy and Toto because of the good witch's kiss.

00:34:27.240 --> 00:34:35.673
So the monkeys picked them up very carefully and carried them to the witch's house.

00:34:35.733 --> 00:34:46.350
The witch saw the kiss on Dorothy's face and was afraid, but she did not tell Dorothy that.

00:34:46.410 --> 00:34:53.898
You must work for me in my house now," she said to the child.

00:34:53.959 --> 00:34:57.922
All day and every day.

00:34:57.982 --> 00:35:05.358
And remember, I am watching you all the time.

00:35:05.418 --> 00:35:12.873
Now Dorothy did not know this, but the red shoes were magic.

00:35:12.934 --> 00:35:16.976
The witch wanted those shoes very much.

00:35:17.036 --> 00:35:20.506
But Dorothy never took them off.

00:35:20.566 --> 00:35:24.560
She took them off when she washed, of course.

00:35:24.620 --> 00:35:27.832
But the witch never went near water.

00:35:27.892 --> 00:35:32.834
She was very, very afraid of water.

00:35:32.894 --> 00:35:39.068
Then, one morning, Dorothy's left shoe fell off.

00:35:39.129 --> 00:35:43.260
The witch hit up the shoe at once.

00:35:43.320 --> 00:35:47.095
This is my shoe now.

00:35:47.155 --> 00:35:48.948
She shouted.

00:35:49.008 --> 00:35:50.929
No, it isn't.

00:35:50.990 --> 00:35:53.372
Shouted Dorothy angrily.

00:35:53.432 --> 00:35:57.435
Give it back to me at once.

00:35:57.455 --> 00:35:59.617
No, said the witch.

00:35:59.677 --> 00:36:04.992
And then she tried to take Dorothy's right shoe too.

00:36:05.052 --> 00:36:11.717
Dorothy loved her red shoes and she was very angry.

00:36:11.777 --> 00:36:15.818
There was a bucket of water near the door.

00:36:15.879 --> 00:36:21.652
Dorothy picked up the bucket and threw the water at the witch.

00:36:21.712 --> 00:36:28.027
The water hit her in the face and she cried out, Help!

00:36:28.087 --> 00:36:29.428
Help!

00:36:29.488 --> 00:36:31.470
The water is killing me!

00:36:31.530 --> 00:36:34.122
The water is!

00:36:34.182 --> 00:36:37.656
And then she disappeared.

00:36:37.716 --> 00:36:44.970
There was only her tall black hat and a long black dress.

00:36:45.031 --> 00:36:51.614
Dorothy looked and looked, but the witch was not there.

00:36:51.674 --> 00:36:56.486
Dorothy picked up her red shoe and put it on.

00:36:56.546 --> 00:37:00.618
Now, how can I help my friend?

00:37:00.678 --> 00:37:05.962
She said, can I call the magic monkey?

00:37:06.022 --> 00:37:11.224
She picked up the witch's black hat and looked at it.

00:37:11.284 --> 00:37:16.132
Perhaps I must wear this magic hat when I speak.

00:37:16.192 --> 00:37:22.672
So she put the hat on and called, Magic Monkeys, come!

00:37:22.732 --> 00:37:26.064
The monkeys arrived in a second.

00:37:26.124 --> 00:37:29.706
Please, can you help my friends?

00:37:29.766 --> 00:37:31.487
asked Dorothy.

00:37:31.548 --> 00:37:34.850
Of course, said the monkeys.

00:37:34.910 --> 00:37:41.984
We must always help the wearer of the magic black hat.

00:37:42.044 --> 00:37:45.300
They broke open the dark cellar.

00:37:45.360 --> 00:37:48.126
and the cowardly lion came out.

00:37:48.186 --> 00:37:53.318
Three at last, he said, thank you.

00:37:53.378 --> 00:38:00.132
Then the monkeys found the scarecrow's clothes and put some new straw in them.

00:38:00.192 --> 00:38:03.254
The scarecrow laughed and jumped.

00:38:03.314 --> 00:38:06.399
Thank you, he said.

00:38:06.459 --> 00:38:13.277
The monkeys mended the tin man and gave him a new oil can.

00:38:13.338 --> 00:38:16.760
He moved his arms and legs.

00:38:16.821 --> 00:38:20.663
I feel wonderful, he said.

00:38:20.723 --> 00:38:22.644
Thank you.

00:38:22.705 --> 00:38:30.380
Dorothy told her friends about the witch and the water, and they were all very happy.

00:38:30.440 --> 00:38:36.564
Toto could not speak, but he jumped up and down very happily.

00:38:36.624 --> 00:38:42.636
Now, said Dorothy, we must go back to the Wizard of Oz.

00:38:42.696 --> 00:38:47.737
Magic monkeys take us to the Emerald City.

00:38:47.798 --> 00:38:53.279
Don't forget the magic black hat, said the Tin Man.

00:38:53.340 --> 00:38:57.382
The monkeys carried them up into the sky.

00:38:57.442 --> 00:39:10.881
And 10 minutes later, the friends were once again at the big green door of the Emerald City.

00:39:10.941 --> 00:39:23.100
Chapter Five, The Old Man from Kansas.

00:39:23.160 --> 00:39:27.302
The little green man opened the door.

00:39:27.362 --> 00:39:30.103
He gave them all glasses.

00:39:30.164 --> 00:39:35.286
Then he took them through the city to the wizard's house.

00:39:35.346 --> 00:39:45.893
There, in the long green room, the friends waited and waited and waited.

00:39:45.953 --> 00:39:53.408
After three hours, the scarecrow said, I'm tired of waiting.

00:39:53.468 --> 00:39:56.040
He called the green man.

00:39:56.100 --> 00:40:02.982
We want to see the wizard now, or we're going to call the magic monkeys.

00:40:03.042 --> 00:40:06.404
Please tell the wizard that.

00:40:06.464 --> 00:40:12.436
The green man went away to speak to the wizard through the door.

00:40:12.496 --> 00:40:16.325
The wizard knew about the magic monkeys.

00:40:16.385 --> 00:40:19.302
and he was very afraid of them.

00:40:19.362 --> 00:40:30.224
So he said to the green man, these people can come and see me at nine o'clock tomorrow morning.

00:40:30.284 --> 00:40:36.285
At nine o'clock, the green man took the friends to the wizard's room.

00:40:36.345 --> 00:40:43.316
They went in and looked all round, but they could not see anybody.

00:40:43.376 --> 00:40:49.672
Then a voice said, I am the wizard of Oz.

00:40:49.732 --> 00:40:55.487
Who are you and what do you want?

00:40:55.548 --> 00:40:59.771
Where are you, Astorthy?

00:40:59.831 --> 00:41:04.825
I am everywhere, but you can't see me.

00:41:04.845 --> 00:41:06.687
Now answer me.

00:41:06.747 --> 00:41:12.548
Who are you and what do you want?

00:41:12.608 --> 00:41:18.670
You know us all," said the Scarecrow.

00:41:18.730 --> 00:41:24.265
You said to me, help Dorothy to kill the witch of the West.

00:41:24.325 --> 00:41:27.257
And you can have some brains.

00:41:27.318 --> 00:41:33.342
Well, the witch is dead, and now I want my brains.

00:41:33.402 --> 00:41:37.806
And I want my heart, said the tin man.

00:41:37.866 --> 00:41:43.210
And I want to be brave, said the cowardly lion.

00:41:43.270 --> 00:41:48.580
And I want to go home to Kansas, said Dorothy.

00:41:48.640 --> 00:41:53.251
Is the witch truly dead?

00:41:53.311 --> 00:41:54.901
asked the voice.

00:41:54.961 --> 00:41:57.362
Yes, said Dorothy.

00:41:57.422 --> 00:42:01.833
I threw a bucket of water over her and she disappeared.

00:42:01.893 --> 00:42:05.413
Very well, said the voice.

00:42:05.473 --> 00:42:07.814
Come again tomorrow.

00:42:07.834 --> 00:42:12.998
I must think about things first and no.

00:42:13.058 --> 00:42:15.403
said the tin man.

00:42:15.463 --> 00:42:18.614
I want my heart now.

00:42:18.674 --> 00:42:23.407
I'm not going to wait another minute," said the scarecrow.

00:42:23.427 --> 00:42:28.950
"'And I'm going to eat you," the lion shouted very angrily.

00:42:29.011 --> 00:42:30.752
Toto was afraid.

00:42:30.812 --> 00:42:36.404
He jumped away from the lion and hid a scream near the wall.

00:42:36.464 --> 00:42:45.127
The scream fell over, and behind it The friend saw an old man with no hair.

00:42:45.187 --> 00:42:50.348
The tin man looked angry and picked up his axe.

00:42:50.408 --> 00:42:52.308
Who are you?

00:42:52.368 --> 00:42:53.969
He said.

00:42:54.029 --> 00:42:56.959
Please, don't hurt me.

00:42:57.019 --> 00:43:00.900
Said the old man in a quiet little voice.

00:43:00.960 --> 00:43:04.141
I'm the wizard of eyes.

00:43:04.201 --> 00:43:10.724
But the wizard of eyes is a big head without a body.

00:43:10.784 --> 00:43:12.398
said Dorothy.

00:43:12.458 --> 00:43:15.900
No, he's a beautiful woman.

00:43:15.960 --> 00:43:17.860
Said the scarecrow.

00:43:17.920 --> 00:43:21.512
Your wrong, said the tin man.

00:43:21.572 --> 00:43:28.036
The wizard of us is a big animal with two heads.

00:43:28.096 --> 00:43:31.128
No, said the lion.

00:43:31.188 --> 00:43:35.160
The wizard is a ball of fire.

00:43:35.220 --> 00:43:38.852
Your all wrong, said the old man.

00:43:38.872 --> 00:43:39.781
I.

00:43:39.841 --> 00:43:41.910
and the wizard.

00:43:41.970 --> 00:43:45.461
Well, I'm not a true wizard.

00:43:45.521 --> 00:43:51.102
Oh, I know a lot of tricks, but I don't know any true magic.

00:43:51.162 --> 00:43:55.223
You see, I'm from Kansas too.

00:43:55.283 --> 00:43:59.934
I went from town to town and did magic tricks.

00:43:59.994 --> 00:44:03.444
And I went up in a big balloon.

00:44:03.504 --> 00:44:06.890
The balloon was always on a rope.

00:44:06.950 --> 00:44:10.216
But one day something went wrong.

00:44:10.276 --> 00:44:14.560
The rope broke and the balloon blew away.

00:44:14.620 --> 00:44:20.042
For a long time the wind carried my balloon across the sky.

00:44:20.102 --> 00:44:25.335
Then I came down here in the country of Oz.

00:44:25.396 --> 00:44:30.859
The people saw my balloon and said, this man is a wizard.

00:44:30.919 --> 00:44:33.290
He comes out of the sky.

00:44:33.350 --> 00:44:37.654
They were afraid of me and wanted to work for me.

00:44:37.714 --> 00:44:44.572
So they built this city for me, and I called it the Emerald City.

00:44:44.632 --> 00:44:51.790
Well, Emeralds are green, so I made green glasses for everybody.

00:44:51.850 --> 00:44:56.274
That's why everything in the city looks green.

00:44:56.334 --> 00:45:00.064
The scarecrow took off his glasses.

00:45:00.124 --> 00:45:04.396
Oh, he said, now I understand.

00:45:04.456 --> 00:45:07.368
The emerald city isn't green.

00:45:07.428 --> 00:45:09.608
It just looks green.

00:45:09.668 --> 00:45:11.720
It's all a trick.

00:45:11.780 --> 00:45:15.391
That's right, said the old man.

00:45:15.451 --> 00:45:20.443
Well, all that happened many years ago.

00:45:20.503 --> 00:45:25.695
I never went out because I was afraid of the two bad witches.

00:45:25.755 --> 00:45:27.566
Now they are dead.

00:45:27.626 --> 00:45:29.668
Thanks to you, Dorothy.

00:45:29.728 --> 00:45:31.909
But I'm very sorry.

00:45:31.970 --> 00:45:34.792
I don't know any true magic.

00:45:34.852 --> 00:45:37.364
So I can't help you.

00:45:37.424 --> 00:45:42.178
You're a very bad man, said Dorothy.

00:45:42.238 --> 00:45:44.249
No, my child.

00:45:44.309 --> 00:45:46.430
I'm a very good man.

00:45:46.491 --> 00:45:49.213
But I am a very bad wizard.

00:45:49.273 --> 00:45:50.744
That's true.

00:45:50.804 --> 00:45:53.306
What about my brains?

00:45:53.366 --> 00:45:55.215
Said the Scarecrow.

00:45:55.275 --> 00:45:57.744
You don't need brains.

00:45:57.804 --> 00:45:59.586
You understand things.

00:45:59.646 --> 00:46:00.866
You can think.

00:46:00.926 --> 00:46:02.478
You learn quickly.

00:46:02.538 --> 00:46:04.578
You're very clever.

00:46:04.638 --> 00:46:09.012
I want brains," said the Scarecrow.

00:46:09.072 --> 00:46:12.404
Very well, said the old man.

00:46:12.464 --> 00:46:15.956
I can give you some brains tomorrow morning.

00:46:16.016 --> 00:46:18.758
What about my heart?

00:46:18.819 --> 00:46:20.730
asked the two men.

00:46:20.790 --> 00:46:25.089
You don't need a heart, said the old man.

00:46:25.149 --> 00:46:30.580
You cry, you love, you feel sorry for people.

00:46:30.640 --> 00:46:35.294
The tin man looked angry and picked up his axe.

00:46:35.354 --> 00:46:38.786
All right, please, don't hurt me.

00:46:38.846 --> 00:46:44.171
Said the old man, I can give you a heart tomorrow morning.

00:46:44.231 --> 00:46:47.393
I want to be brave.

00:46:47.454 --> 00:46:49.895
Said the cowardly lion.

00:46:49.956 --> 00:46:52.528
But you are brave.

00:46:52.588 --> 00:46:55.350
You do a lot of brave things.

00:46:55.410 --> 00:46:58.272
No, no, don't eat me.

00:46:58.332 --> 00:47:00.713
Come here tomorrow morning.

00:47:00.773 --> 00:47:03.844
I'm going to make you brave.

00:47:03.904 --> 00:47:06.346
What about Toto and me?

00:47:06.406 --> 00:47:08.018
asked Dorothy.

00:47:08.078 --> 00:47:12.180
We can go up in my balloon, said the wizard.

00:47:12.240 --> 00:47:15.292
The wind blew us here from Kansas.

00:47:15.352 --> 00:47:20.094
Perhaps it can blow us back to Kansas again.

00:47:20.154 --> 00:47:25.693
The next morning, the friends came again to the wizard's room.

00:47:25.753 --> 00:47:27.899
The old man was ready.

00:47:27.959 --> 00:47:36.675
He took a bottle with brains on it in big green letters and carefully opened the scarecrow's head.

00:47:36.735 --> 00:47:38.216
Don't move.

00:47:38.276 --> 00:47:41.158
I'm putting your brains in, he said.

00:47:41.218 --> 00:47:42.399
There.

00:47:42.459 --> 00:47:45.992
Now you're the cleverest scarecrow in Oz.

00:47:46.052 --> 00:47:48.512
The scarecrow thanked him.

00:47:48.572 --> 00:47:55.280
Next, the wizard gave the tin man a small red heart.

00:47:55.340 --> 00:47:59.194
where this always," he said.

00:47:59.254 --> 00:48:05.835
The tin man was very happy and thanked the wizard again and again.

00:48:05.895 --> 00:48:12.426
Then the old man took a bottle with bee brave on it.

00:48:12.486 --> 00:48:16.707
Drink this, he said to the cowardly lion.

00:48:16.767 --> 00:48:19.994
The lion drank.

00:48:20.054 --> 00:48:23.322
I feel brave."

00:48:23.382 --> 00:48:26.824
He shouted, very, very brave.

00:48:26.844 --> 00:48:28.996
Thank you.

00:48:29.056 --> 00:48:32.208
The wizard smiled at them.

00:48:32.268 --> 00:48:35.980
You didn't need my magic, he said.

00:48:36.040 --> 00:48:39.782
But you're all happy now, and that's a good thing.

00:48:39.842 --> 00:48:44.786
Now, Dorothy, he said, come and see my balloon.

00:48:44.846 --> 00:48:46.337
It's all ready.

00:48:46.397 --> 00:48:49.192
I mended it last night.

00:48:49.252 --> 00:48:53.996
They went out into the garden behind the wizard's house.

00:48:54.056 --> 00:48:56.818
The balloon was very big.

00:48:56.878 --> 00:49:02.870
There was a small box under it, and the wizard of Oz jumped into the box.

00:49:02.930 --> 00:49:04.951
Come on, Dorothy.

00:49:05.011 --> 00:49:08.292
He shouted, we're going to Kansas.

00:49:08.352 --> 00:49:11.254
Say goodbye to your friends.

00:49:11.314 --> 00:49:17.966
Dorothy kissed the scarecrow, the lion, and the tin man and said goodbye.

00:49:18.026 --> 00:49:20.349
Come on, Toto, she said.

00:49:20.409 --> 00:49:22.762
We're going home to Kansas.

00:49:22.822 --> 00:49:26.104
We're going to see Aunt Anne and Uncle Henry.

00:49:26.164 --> 00:49:30.216
But just then, Toto saw a cat.

00:49:30.276 --> 00:49:34.620
He jumped out of Dorothy's arms and ran after it.

00:49:34.680 --> 00:49:43.962
Toto called Dorothy and she began to run after him.

00:49:44.022 --> 00:49:56.456
Chapter six, East West Holmes Beth.

00:49:56.516 --> 00:50:01.578
Leave the dog and come quickly, shouted the wizard.

00:50:01.638 --> 00:50:03.829
The rope's going to break.

00:50:03.889 --> 00:50:06.990
Dorothy picked Toto up and ran.

00:50:07.050 --> 00:50:09.371
Wait, she shouted.

00:50:09.432 --> 00:50:13.762
But before she got there, the rope did break.

00:50:13.822 --> 00:50:19.424
And the balloon went up, up, up into the sky.

00:50:19.484 --> 00:50:24.368
They heard the old man's voice very far away.

00:50:24.428 --> 00:50:29.590
Ask the witch of the south.

00:50:29.650 --> 00:50:37.666
Then the balloon disappeared and nobody saw the Wizard of Oz again.

00:50:37.726 --> 00:50:41.566
Dorothy began to cry.

00:50:41.627 --> 00:50:45.357
How can I get home now?"

00:50:45.417 --> 00:50:53.000
Put on the magic black hat, said the scarecrow, and asked the magic monkeys for help.

00:50:53.060 --> 00:50:58.542
Perhaps they can find the witch of the south and bring her here.

00:50:58.602 --> 00:51:02.424
Clever scarecrow said Dorothy.

00:51:02.484 --> 00:51:07.696
She put on the magic hat and called for the magic monkey.

00:51:07.756 --> 00:51:17.854
When they arrived, she said, Find the Witch of the South and bring her here to the Emerald City.

00:51:17.914 --> 00:51:26.868
And five minutes later, a beautiful woman with long red hair arrived.

00:51:26.928 --> 00:51:33.032
I am Glinda, the Witch of the South, she said.

00:51:33.092 --> 00:51:36.953
What can I do for you, my child?

00:51:37.014 --> 00:51:41.864
I want to go home to Kansas, said Dorothy.

00:51:41.924 --> 00:51:45.024
Please, can you help me?

00:51:45.084 --> 00:51:47.456
Ask your shoes.

00:51:47.516 --> 00:51:52.598
Smiled the good witch, but Dorothy did not understand.

00:51:52.658 --> 00:51:58.372
Your red shoes, said Glinda, are magic shoes.

00:51:58.432 --> 00:52:00.863
They can carry you home.

00:52:00.923 --> 00:52:09.478
Just close your eyes and say east, west, home, west, then jump.

00:52:09.538 --> 00:52:11.728
Oh, thank you.

00:52:11.788 --> 00:52:13.858
cried Dorothy happily.

00:52:13.918 --> 00:52:17.662
She kissed her friends and said goodbye again.

00:52:17.722 --> 00:52:22.594
Then she picked up Toto and closed her eyes.

00:52:22.654 --> 00:52:28.480
East, West, home's best, she said and jumped.

00:52:28.540 --> 00:52:34.954
There was a noise like a wind and suddenly Dorothy was in the sky.

00:52:35.014 --> 00:52:40.752
The red shoes fell off her feet and she never saw them again.

00:52:40.812 --> 00:52:55.432
When she opened her eyes, there she was, back in Kansas, and there were Antem and Uncle Henry in a field by a new little house.

00:52:55.492 --> 00:52:58.744
Dorothy, cried Antem.

00:52:58.804 --> 00:53:02.376
She ran and took Dorothy in her arms.

00:53:02.436 --> 00:53:05.827
Oh, Dorothy, what happened to you?

00:53:05.887 --> 00:53:08.318
And where did you come from?

00:53:08.379 --> 00:53:17.311
From the country of Oz, said Dorothy, but I'm home again now, and I'm so happy.

